 ### Adaptive Number of Updates
-An adaptive system to adjust the number of opacity map updates ($k$) per frame based on performance history to balance rendering speed and occlusion detection overhead. The system starts with an empirically determined $k$ (typically 9) and maintains a performance history window. Every $n$-th frame (e.g., $n=10$), it polls the performance using the number in range $[k-hw, k+hw]$ that has not been updated for the longest. The performance function is $p = v - c \cdot k$, where $v$ is the percentage of voxels culled and clipped, and $c$ is a constant (0.02 for tested datasets) [S1]. When all slots are valid, the slot with the best performance becomes the new center [S1].
